# ── BMAD (personal, installer-managed) ────────────────────────────
_bmad/config.user.toml

# Upstream VARIABLE font builds, fetched only to replay the shipped
# faces' derivation (`make fonts` / `make fonts-verify`, D-2.2.4). They
# are inputs, not artifacts: ~20 MB of sources for the ~11 MB of static
# faces that actually ship and ARE committed. Each face's NOTICE.md
# records the release URL and the sha256 to fetch them by.
/.font-sources/

# Local fontgen toolchain (pinned Python 3.12.13 + fontTools 4.63.0), never committed
/.fontgen-venv/
# Playwright output is disposable; Story 6.7 attaches a bounded JSON manifest
# to its run rather than retaining PDFs or platform binaries in this tree.
folio-designer/test-results/
folio-designer/playwright-report/

# Python bytecode from the BMAD skill scripts, regenerated on every run.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ── .NET (folio-dotnet, client-libraries story 6) ─────────────────
# MSBuild/NuGet intermediates. `bin/`, `*.dll`, `*.so` and `*.dylib` are
# already ignored above by the Go section, which is what keeps the native
# library out of the tree; these are the .NET-specific leftovers.
obj/
*.user
TestResults/
# folio-dotnet/build/ holds the two BUILD SCRIPTS, not build output, so the
# generic `build/` rule above (line 28, a Node convention) must not swallow
# them. Only the artifacts they produce are ignored, below.
!/folio-dotnet/build/
!/folio-dotnet/build/*.sh
!/folio-dotnet/build/*.ps1
# Story 7's MSBuild targets, SHIPPED INSIDE THE NUGET PACKAGE. It is authored
# source like the two scripts beside it, not build output.
!/folio-dotnet/build/*.targets
# The native library and the cgo-generated header build-native.sh writes.
# NEVER committed: the host library is a development aid and the Windows
# DLLs are CI artifacts, both rebuilt from folio-go/cshared on demand.
/folio-dotnet/build/native/
# Story 7's pack output and the consumer workspace run-consumers.ps1 builds
# into: a .nupkg, six consumer builds and their copies. All rebuilt on demand
# from the sources beside them, and a tracked .nupkg would be a second source
# of truth for what the package contains.
/artifacts/
# And a .nupkg anywhere: the documented pack command can be pointed elsewhere,
# and a 42 MB package is never something this repository should carry.
*.nupkg

# Local `go build` output of the c-shared entry point; the real artifacts
# are built into folio-dotnet/build/native by build-native.sh.
/folio-go/cshared/cmd/folio8/folio8
